From: AlexanderNyr <131390634+AlexanderNyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:13:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] W5 update: inline CSS

WEBVIEW_PLAN.md phase W5 (D4 subset):
- wv_css.{h,c}: declaration parser (malformed decl never discards its
  block), selectors tag/#id/.class/type.class/comma lists (no
  combinators, later wins, inline wins), colours #rgb/#rrggbb/16 names,
  lengths px, margin/padding 1-2-4 forms, border width; unknown props
  ignored, unknown selectors skipped (CSS error recovery)
- layout computes styles per element: display none/block, color
  inherited into block text, background-color, width, height, per-side
  margin/padding over UA, border painted, font-weight through nesting,
  text-align with line tracking (shift on wrap and at block close)
- host gate: test_wv_css.c 71 checks: style=color:#f00 red text;
  malformed decl keeps the block; EVERY D4 property changes the output;
  selectors precedence; display:none; 4-value margins; border pixels;
  text-align offsets; no-CSS builds hash identically to W4; 500 fuzz
- bugs found: selector matcher infinite loop on trailing comma; #rgb
  channel shift wrong; leading-whitespace values failed; type.class not
  matched -- fixed with regressions
- STACK SAFETY: wv_css_build used a 64 KiB stack buffer and overflowed
  the real user stack in QEMU ([GUARD] user stack overflow) -- reworked
  to parse text nodes in place, no large stack buffers anywhere
- QEMU gate: 5-rule <style> demo page: css smoke: PASS
  (styled=0x4d394d5c, plain=0x2f39d54f); reference hash 0x4D394D5C
  identical on host and guest; test_webview.sh asserts (14 checks)
- webview.elf ~175 KB; make test-unit green
